---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import { SITE, BELIEFS } from '../data/site';
import { personSchema, profilePageSchema } from '../lib/schema';
---
<Base title="About" type="profile"
  description="About Manish Tripathi: from M&A research at S&P Global to leading power-market data at Aurora Energy Research. How he works and what he believes about data."
  schema={[personSchema(), profilePageSchema(`${SITE.url}/about/`)]}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About Manish Tripathi</h1>
      <p class="desc">{SITE.positioning}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="cols">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>For years, I thought my job was to find insights. Then I realised insights only matter when they change a decision.</p>
        <p>I spent eleven years in research at S&amp;P Global Market Intelligence, working on M&amp;A data and onboarding more than 40 researchers across four offices to the same quality standards. I then studied Business Analytics, Machine Learning and Advanced Statistics at the Indian School of Business, where I made the Dean’s List.</p>
        <p>After that I worked in growth analytics at SkillGigs, leading a team of three analysts, and in marketing analytics at Amplify Analytix, building dbt and BigQuery pipelines and customer models on Databricks.</p>
        <p>Since January 2025 I have been a Product Manager at Aurora Energy Research. I own the historical power-market dashboards, the licensing and governance of the data behind them, and the India analytics team that keeps that data clean.</p>
        <p>I am based in {SITE.location}, and open to senior product and data leadership roles, advisory conversations and consulting.</p>
        <p><a href="/cv/">Read my CV</a> or <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <img class="portrait" src={SITE.photo} alt="Portrait of Manish Tripathi" width="176" height="176" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="beliefs">
      <SectionHead num="01" title="Three beliefs" id="beliefs" />
      <ol class="beliefs prose">
        {BELIEFS.map((b) => <li>{b}</li>)}
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
